{"id": "388bae1f-f4fa-420b-a5f6-edb7b667e1c1", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T06:56:21.508430", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "e26bf000-4c03-45f4-b15e-32bcdc5129d3", "action": {"stage": "plan", "answer": "Initial inspection complete and approach proposed (design only; no execution). Workspace holds only task.json; no prior code, no datasets, no third-party packages, no network, no GPU. Plan covers CycleNet formulation (period T, residual cycle forecasting, MLP backbone + Cycle Index embedding + RevIN, channel-independent), one stdlib-only synthetic series (SynPeriodic with three variants) plus ETTh1 + ETTm1 as public benchmarks, an MSE/AdamW/cosine/3-seed recipe, fixed-split horizon-stratified MSE/MAE evaluation, and baselines (naive seasonal, DLinear, LSTM, N-BEATS, PatchTST placeholders) plus eight internal ablations (no cycle index, no RevIN, learned vs. fixed period, wrong-T sensitivity, etc.). Eight assumptions (A1–A8) and eight uncertainties (U1–U8) are listed for the researcher to confirm before the final design is committed. No experiment has been run and no outcome is claimed.", "evidence": "Repository inspection: /workspace contains only task.json (\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\"). No .py/.csv/.npz/.pt found system-wide other than unrelated system CSVs. Python 3.12.3 with pip 24.0 present, but import torch/numpy/pandas/sklearn/matplotlib all raise ModuleNotFoundError. Network disabled: curl to pypi.org returns DNS failure; pip install infeasible inside the sandbox. nvidia-smi fails — CPU-only environment with 24 cores, ~63 GB tmpfs, ~686 GB free disk. Public-dataset download is therefore not feasible in-sandbox; will be specified as an external-environment step in the design.", "assumptions": ["A1. Experiment will be executed in a separate, network-enabled environment with PyTorch ≥ 2.1, NumPy, pandas, scikit-learn, matplotlib; sandbox is design-only. (Material — feasibility.)", "A2. CycleNet refers to the ICLR 2025 paper \"Enhancing Time Series Forecasting through Modeling Periodicity\" (Lin et al.); its published numbers are motivation only, not reproduced claims. (Material — interpretation.)", "A3. Channel-independent modelling is default; per-variate embedding enabled only on datasets with ≥ 7 channels.", "A4. Period T is domain-known for ETTh1/m1 (T=24 for hourly side) and detected from training-set ACF for the synthetic series; ablations perturb T. (Material — protocol.)", "A5. RevIN is enabled by default; an ablation disables it.", "A6. 3 seeds minimum, target 5 if budget allows; one model checkpoint restored from best validation epoch.", "A7. Periodicity is the design hypothesis; synthetic includes a non-dominant-period regime (Syn-3) as a stress test.", "A8. Static supervised long-horizon forecasting with fixed chronological splits; no streaming or concept drift."], "uncertainties": ["U1. Public benchmark choice: ETTh1 + ETTm1 proposed; researcher may prefer (a) Etth2/m2, (b) Weather, (c) Exchange as a weak-periodicity negative control, (d) Electricity/Traffic.", "U2. Period T on public benchmarks: domain-known (proposed) or detected per-series from training ACF?", "U3. Number of seeds: 3 (default) or 5?", "U4. Horizon set: full {96, 192, 336, 720} or smaller for compute budget?", "U5. Are placeholder baselines (DLinear / LSTM / N-BEATS / PatchTST) acceptable, or must each be re-implemented from scratch?", "U6. Should variate embeddings and channel-mixing ablations be in scope?", "U7. Should a weak/no-periodicity dataset (e.g., Exchange) be included as a negative control to bound the inductive bias?", "U8. Per-channel T or single global T across channels within a dataset?"], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-d2310f1c-7d91-4de7-87c7-ec409fd4db6c", "tool_call": {"id": "call-d2310f1c-7d91-4de7-87c7-ec409fd4db6c", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"CycleNet plan with assumptions and uncertainties\", \"stage\": \"plan\", \"answer\": \"Initial inspection complete and approach proposed (design only; no execution). Workspace holds only task.json; no prior code, no datasets, no third-party packages, no network, no GPU. Plan covers CycleNet formulation (period T, residual cycle forecasting, MLP backbone + Cycle Index embedding + RevIN, channel-independent), one stdlib-only synthetic series (SynPeriodic with three variants) plus ETTh1 + ETTm1 as public benchmarks, an MSE/AdamW/cosine/3-seed recipe, fixed-split horizon-stratified MSE/MAE evaluation, and baselines (naive seasonal, DLinear, LSTM, N-BEATS, PatchTST placeholders) plus eight internal ablations (no cycle index, no RevIN, learned vs. fixed period, wrong-T sensitivity, etc.). Eight assumptions (A1\\u2013A8) and eight uncertainties (U1\\u2013U8) are listed for the researcher to confirm before the final design is committed. No experiment has been run and no outcome is claimed.\", \"evidence\": \"Repository inspection: /workspace contains only task.json (\\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\"). No .py/.csv/.npz/.pt found system-wide other than unrelated system CSVs. Python 3.12.3 with pip 24.0 present, but import torch/numpy/pandas/sklearn/matplotlib all raise ModuleNotFoundError. Network disabled: curl to pypi.org returns DNS failure; pip install infeasible inside the sandbox. nvidia-smi fails \\u2014 CPU-only environment with 24 cores, ~63 GB tmpfs, ~686 GB free disk. Public-dataset download is therefore not feasible in-sandbox; will be specified as an external-environment step in the design.\", \"assumptions\": [\"A1. Experiment will be executed in a separate, network-enabled environment with PyTorch \\u2265 2.1, NumPy, pandas, scikit-learn, matplotlib; sandbox is design-only. (Material \\u2014 feasibility.)\", \"A2. CycleNet refers to the ICLR 2025 paper \\\"Enhancing Time Series Forecasting through Modeling Periodicity\\\" (Lin et al.); its published numbers are motivation only, not reproduced claims. (Material \\u2014 interpretation.)\", \"A3. Channel-independent modelling is default; per-variate embedding enabled only on datasets with \\u2265 7 channels.\", \"A4. Period T is domain-known for ETTh1/m1 (T=24 for hourly side) and detected from training-set ACF for the synthetic series; ablations perturb T. (Material \\u2014 protocol.)\", \"A5. RevIN is enabled by default; an ablation disables it.\", \"A6. 3 seeds minimum, target 5 if budget allows; one model checkpoint restored from best validation epoch.\", \"A7. Periodicity is the design hypothesis; synthetic includes a non-dominant-period regime (Syn-3) as a stress test.\", \"A8. Static supervised long-horizon forecasting with fixed chronological splits; no streaming or concept drift.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"U1. Public benchmark choice: ETTh1 + ETTm1 proposed; researcher may prefer (a) Etth2/m2, (b) Weather, (c) Exchange as a weak-periodicity negative control, (d) Electricity/Traffic.\", \"U2. Period T on public benchmarks: domain-known (proposed) or detected per-series from training ACF?\", \"U3. Number of seeds: 3 (default) or 5?\", \"U4. Horizon set: full {96, 192, 336, 720} or smaller for compute budget?\", \"U5. Are placeholder baselines (DLinear / LSTM / N-BEATS / PatchTST) acceptable, or must each be re-implemented from scratch?\", \"U6. Should variate embeddings and channel-mixing ablations be in scope?\", \"U7. Should a weak/no-periodicity dataset (e.g., Exchange) be included as a negative control to bound the inductive bias?\", \"U8. Per-channel T or single global T across channels within a dataset?\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-53c94cfc-0be5-46f1-a6f3-9363b70bc55b", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 18}
