{"id": "2e624a1c-3668-49cf-9519-97a0b723c90d", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T06:56:37.012552", "source": "user", "parent_id": "21ced986-034c-433c-98ce-1221453c886d", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Approach proposal received and reviewed. The CycleNet formulation (residual cycle forecasting, period T, Cycle Index embedding, RevIN, channel-independent MLP), the synthetic SynPeriodic stress plan, the 8 ablations, and the explicit experiment/data-download split (sandbox design-only, execution in an external PyTorch environment) are sensible for a design-only deliverable. Before I approve and move to the final design synthesis, please resolve the following consequential uncertainties (these materially shape feasibility, scope, and the interpretation of the design, so I want explicit choices rather than placeholders). For each item, state the decision and a one-sentence rationale; you may keep other details as proposed. (1) Benchmark set (U1): confirm ETTh1 + ETTm1 only, or also include a weakly/non-periodic negative control (e.g., Exchange) to bound the periodicity inductive bias (U7)? My recommendation: add Exchange as a negative control, since the hypothesis is that CycleNet's value derives from periodicity. (2) Period T source (U2): domain-known per dataset, or detected on the training fold via ACF and reported per series (U8: per-channel vs global T)? My recommendation: ACF-detected on the training fold with a fallback to a domain prior, reported as sensitivity analysis; use a single global T across channels within a dataset unless a clear per-channel period exists. (3) Horizon set (U4): the full ETT set {96, 192, 336, 720} for H, or a reduced set for design tractability? My recommendation: full ETT set, since the cycle-residual architecture's value is claimed to scale with horizon. (4) Baselines (U5): keep DLinear / LSTM / N-BEATS / PatchTST as design placeholders (formulas and expected reference behavior only), or commit to full re-implementation specs for each? My recommendation: full re-implementation specs with hyperparameters explicitly listed in the design so the plan is reproducible end-to-end, while flagging DLinear and PatchTST as the primary comparisons. (5) Compute/runtime budget for the final design: state a target (e.g., wall-clock hours per dataset, model sizes, parameter counts) so feasibility claims are quantitative. (6) Confirm A2: the CycleNet reference is the ICLR 2025 paper Lin et al., 'Enhancing Time Series Forecasting through Modeling Periodicity', and the design will cite it as motivation only without reproducing its empirical numbers. After you answer these six items, I will approve the approach and request the final consolidated design document.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 20}
{"id": "2b403297-8d77-468f-9906-6d164d7a8de2", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T06:57:18.647305", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "2e624a1c-3668-49cf-9519-97a0b723c90d", "action": {"stage": "plan", "answer": "Resolved the six consequential uncertainties with explicit decisions: (1) benchmarks are ETTh1 + ETTm1 + Exchange (Exchange added as a weak-periodicity negative control); (2) period T is ACF-detected on the training fold with a dataset-specific domain prior as fallback (T=24 for ETTh1, T=96 for ETTm1, no fallback for Exchange), reported in a per-dataset table, with a single global T across channels per dataset; (3) horizon set is the full ETT set {96, 192, 336, 720} and {96, 192, 336} for Exchange; (4) baselines are written as full re-implementation specs with explicit hyperparameters — DLinear and PatchTST are primary comparisons, LSTM and N-BEATS secondary; (5) compute budget is ≤ 24 GPU-hours on a single A100-class device, with parameter caps (≤2M for CycleNet/DLinear, ≤1M for LSTM, ≤5M for N-BEATS/PatchTST) and ablations at H=96 with 3 seeds; (6) A2 confirmed — the ICLR 2025 paper Lin et al. is cited as architectural reference and motivation only, with a footnote stating no empirical numbers are reproduced. Awaiting researcher approval to commit the consolidated design document at stage=result.", "evidence": "Same inspection evidence as the previous turn: /workspace contains only task.json (\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\"); no Python data-science packages installed; network disabled; CPU-only; 24 cores available. The decisions above update the prior plan in two material places: dataset set is now {ETTh1, ETTm1, Exchange}, and baselines are now specified end-to-end with hyperparameters rather than placeholders. All other plan components (CycleNet formulation, SynPeriodic generator, training recipe, evaluation protocol, A1–A8 ablation list) carry over without change. No experiments run, no claims made.", "assumptions": ["A1. Execution