arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Resolved 6 uncertainties with explicit choices\", \"stage\": \"plan\", \"answer\": \"Resolved the six consequential uncertainties with explicit decisions: (1) benchmarks are ETTh1 + ETTm1 + Exchange (Exchange added as a weak-periodicity negative control); (2) period T is ACF-detected on the training fold with a dataset-specific domain prior as fallback (T=24 for ETTh1, T=96 for ETTm1, no fallback for Exchange), reported in a per-dataset table, with a single global T across channels per dataset; (3) horizon set is the full ETT set {96, 192, 336, 720} and {96, 192, 336} for Exchange; (4) baselines are written as full re-implementation specs with explicit hyperparameters \\u2014 DLinear and PatchTST are primary comparisons, LSTM and N-BEATS secondary; (5) compute budget is \\u2264 24 GPU-hours on a single A100-class device, with parameter caps (\\u22642M for CycleNet/DLinear, \\u22641M for LSTM, \\u22645M for N-BEATS/PatchTST) and ablations at H=96 with 3 seeds; (6) A2 confirmed \\u2014 the ICLR 2025 paper Lin et al. is cited as architectural reference and motivation only, with a footnote stating no empirical numbers are reproduced. Awaiting researcher approval to commit the consolidated design document at stage=result.\", \"evidence\": \"Same inspection evidence as the previous turn: /workspace contains only task.json (\\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"); no Python data-science packages installed; network disabled; CPU-only; 24 cores available. The decisions above update the prior plan in two material places: dataset set is now {ETTh1, ETTm1, Exchange}, and baselines are now specified end-to-end with hyperparameters rather than placeholders. All other plan components (CycleNet formulation, SynPeriodic generator, training recipe, evaluation protocol, A1\\u2013A8 ablation list) carry over without change. No experiments run, no claims made.\", \"assumptions\": [\"A1. Execution happens in an external, network-enabled PyTorch environment; this sandbox is design-only.\", \"A2. CycleNet reference: Lin et al., ICLR 2025, cited for definitions and architecture only; no empirical numbers reproduced.\", \"A3. Channel-independent modelling default; variate embedding off unless the dataset has \\u2265 7 channels.\", \"A4. T is ACF-detected on the training fold only; fallback is T=24 (ETTh1), T=96 (ETTm1), no fallback for Exchange; reported per dataset; ablations A4 and A5 perturb T.\", \"A5. RevIN enabled by default; one ablation disables it.\", \"A6. 5 seeds for main runs, 3 seeds for ablations; best validation-epoch checkpoint restored.\", \"A7. Static supervised long-horizon forecasting; fixed chronological splits; no streaming, no concept drift.\", \"A8. Horizon set: ETTh1/ETTm1 use {96, 192, 336, 720}; Exchange uses {96, 192, 336} due to series length.\", \"A9. Compute envelope: \\u2264 24 GPU-hours on one A100-class device; model parameter caps \\u2264 2M (CycleNet, DLinear), \\u2264 1M (LSTM), \\u2264 5M (N-BEATS, PatchTST).\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"U1. Benchmark set now fixed as ETTh1 + ETTm1 + Exchange.\", \"U2. T gets a per-dataset table of detected/fallback values; no remaining ambiguity unless ACF detection is unstable, which A4 is built to detect.\", \"U3. Seeds: main runs use 5, ablations use 3 \\u2014 confirmed.\", \"U4. Horizon sets are dataset-dependent as in A8 \\u2014 confirmed.\", \"U5. Baselines are now specific re-implementation specs \\u2014 confirmed.\", \"U6. Variate embeddings remain off unless \\u2265 7 channels; deemed in scope but only cycled on for datasets where applicable.\", \"U7. Exchange as negative control \\u2014 confirmed.\", \"U8. Single global T across channels per dataset \\u2014 confirmed; per-channel T is recovered through ablation, not as a default.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-255a8292-4dd1-4c4a-a29e-70fb6f2e79d4", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 21}
