{"id": "b02c8b57-21d6-4489-bcb1-a2443180620a", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T06:57:31.626509", "source": "user", "parent_id": "22570b47-c0d7-46e1-8f64-338624b376fa", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Approach approved. The following decisions are now committed and supersede any prior placeholders: (U1) benchmark set = {ETTh1, ETTm1, Exchange}, with Exchange as a weak/non-periodic negative control; (U2) period T is ACF-detected on the training fold with dataset-specific fallbacks (24 for ETTh1, 96 for ETTm1, none for Exchange), one global T across channels per dataset, and a per-dataset T table reported in the design; (U4/U8) horizon set {96, 192, 336, 720} for ETTh1/ETTm1 and {96, 192, 336} for Exchange; (U5) baselines are fully-specified re-implementations with explicit hyperparameters (DLinear and PatchTST as primary comparisons, LSTM and N-BEATS as secondary); (compute) single-GPU A100-class envelope of <=24 hours with parameter caps (CycleNet/DLinear <=2M, LSTM <=1M, N-BEATS/PatchTST <=5M), main runs 5 seeds, ablations 3 seeds at H=96; (A2) CycleNet reference is Lin et al., ICLR 2025, cited for architecture and motivation only with an explicit footnote that no empirical numbers are reproduced. All other plan components carry forward unchanged: CycleNet formulation (residual cycle forecasting, Cycle Index embedding, RevIN, channel-independent MLP), SynPeriodic toy generator with the three regimes, MSE/AdamW/cosine training recipe, fixed chronological splits with horizon-stratified MSE/MAE evaluation, and the eight internal ablations. Now produce the final consolidated experiment design document. As a design-only deliverable, it must include: (a) research question and hypotheses with explicit pre-registered predictions, (b) the full CycleNet model spec (inputs/outputs, lookback L, cycle decomposition, embedding table, MLP widths/depths/activations/normalization, RevIN placement, chann